From e85820376b67919b6e312ca98cd3d9dd8904f663 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Build <build@local>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 13:55:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] riscv: complete sched_ext integration and add lazy vector
 restore

Complete the sched_ext port integration for the vendor 6.6 scheduler and cgroup interfaces, increase the dispatch loop budget, and retain the local scheduler header needed by the core implementation.

Add an opt-in per-CPU userspace Vector owner. Keep eager saves as the memory fallback, elide only the v0-v31 payload restore on a valid owner hit, and always restore Vector CSRs. Cover kernel Vector use, KVM, CPU power transitions, signal restore, ptrace and exec invalidation, with debugfs counters and a context selftest.

Also fix the bcmdhd source include path for out-of-tree builds and the host libbpf const qualifier needed by clean kernel builds.
